CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11 --verbosity 9
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ branch not taken: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^Unwinding loop main\.0
--
N5008 [class.bit]/4: simplify_typecast did not fold a constant of a
bit-field type whose underlying type is an enumeration tag (to_integer
needs the namespace for it), so the guard `(int)s.type == 7' stayed
symbolic and symbolic execution unwound the 1000 iterations of the untaken
loop.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its
WRONG assertion.
